  "description": "Curated held-out golden cases for the mention-decoration pipeline (issue #2516). One case is one pasuk; `mentions` are the decorations a human curator would persist for it. `text` is the normalized surface (diacritics stripped, maqaf as space) of the joined segment values so the case stays readable; a consistency test re-derives it from the canonical dump. `name` is the intended entry unique-name key; `name_alternates` accepts synonym-equivalent keys. `type` is the entity_type a curator would record; `type_alternates` records genuine taxonomy ambiguity (e.g. a land that is also a people). Cases are deliberately adversarial — they concentrate on the categories the issue requires, so the measured numbers describe gap coverage, not unbiased corpus accuracy.",
  "categories": {
    "ordinary-nouns": "Pesukim dominated by common words; any decoration is a false positive.",
    "recall-gap": "Mentions the lexical tier cannot see (e.g. אלהים is not morphhb-tagged as a proper noun).",
    "ambiguity": "Same spelling, different referent by context (ישראל person vs nation, מצרים person vs land).",
    "multi-word": "Compound names (בית אל, בת שבע, אור כשדים, אלון מורה) — covered and missed.",
    "prefixes": "Fused inseparable prefixes (ו/ב/ל/מ/ה/ש, directive ה) on the surface.",
    "vocalization": "Niqqud/taamim present on the source segments.",
    "qri-ktiv": "Ktiv/qri pairs — two displayed surfaces of one logical word.",
    "gentilic": "Gentilic forms typed NATION.",
